  "review": {"authority": "first_party_published", "method": "dual_reviewer", "reviewers": [{"id": "spec-registry-rebuild-lane-20260819", "reviewedOn": "2026-08-19"}, {"id": "normalization-review-20260829", "reviewedOn": "2026-08-29"}], "notes": "Normalized from the 2026-08-19 rebuild research. Three adjudications carry into this revision. The published \"JPG files\" instruction and the form's own .jpg/.jpeg/.png/.gif accept string are both recorded, as a required rule and an allowed rule, because they disagree and the source of truth at submit time is unobservable; export therefore narrows to JPEG. The 3MB cap is published but is not enforced in the browser, so it is recorded as the agency's rule rather than as form behaviour. The weekly Thursday open call attributed to Q by a third-party directory is deliberately absent: Q's own site publishes no open-call schedule, its only first-party statement (2019) says calls were on hold, and the directory's addresses do not match Q's. The form's CM/INCH measurement-unit selector has no taxonomy field and is not represented here."}
